<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-6028] Kylin5 encounters metadata anomalies when concurrently submitting build/refresh tasks</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-6028</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In Kylin5, when two incremental build tasks with the same time range for the same model are submitted concurrently, both requests succeed. However, only one segment is created for the model, while two build tasks are created, which is inconsistent with expectations. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Further verification shows that the same issue occurs when concurrently refreshing the same segment. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Additional testing reveals that submitting build/refresh tasks concurrently for a model may result in issues, regardless of whether these tasks conflict or not.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13609008">KYLIN-6028</key>
            <summary>Kylin5 encounters metadata anomalies when concurrently submitting build/refresh tasks</summary>
